infographic hierarchy-tree-curved-line-rounded-rect-node
data
  root
    label Shard-key strategy: every win buys one failure mode
    children
      - label Hash — shard = hash(key) mod N
        children
          - label Win: uniform on uniform keys
          - label Risk: hot shard on skewed keys; changing N moves most rows
      - label Range — each shard owns a key range
        children
          - label Win: natural for time-series; add a shard at the tail
          - label Risk: hot tail — newest records all land on one shard
      - label List — explicit key to shard map
        children
          - label Win: maximum control
          - label Risk: does not scale to millions of keys
      - label Directory — external lookup table
        children
          - label Win: move individual tenants by updating one row
          - label Risk: lookup cost per request; map is tier-1 infrastructure
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
